WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.829
Slash ship takes a change from a
local check to a pushed commit.

2
00:00:04.829 --> 00:00:09.120
Here, the change adds a shout
flag to a tiny command line app.

3
00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:12.773
Pi runs the tests, stages three files,

4
00:00:12.773 --> 00:00:16.315
and pushes a focused commit
to a disposable remote.

5
00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:21.733
The hosted CI response is a labeled
fixture for the exact commit that arrived.

6
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.077
When you ship, keep the local
result and hosted status separate.

7
00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:39.340
Check the commit that
actually reached the remote.
